                <pb facs="0344" n="252" xml:id="pg252"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-15"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 171.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to the cablegram received to-day I
                    do not understand what the Department requests. I forwarded in dispatch No. 166,
                    of December 5, 1899, all the information that was in my possession concerning
                    the Ozama Bridge award. I am awaiting instructions from the Department in
                    reference to it, and what steps I shall take in the recognition of the present
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Up to the present time I have received no information from that Government of its
                    existence, nor has either of my colleagues here. I do not care to assume this
                    responsibility without full instructions from the Department.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
